+   * {@code aa <b>bb</b> cc} the PDF holds {@code aa}, {@code cc}, {@code bb}. The page looks the same, but text
+   * extraction then reads {@code bb} apart from its neighbours: a comma after a bold word becomes a word of its own
+   * and the same page yields different words than html-pdf's (task T11). A plain span adds no box decoration and does
